+# Bug Fix: Category deletion removes products and breaks references
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Fixed**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Assessment**: ./assessment.md
+- **Status**: applied
+
+## Summary
+
+Category deletion now detaches deleted-subtree categories from affected products and persists the products, including products left with no categories. The delete facade uses the store-aware not-found lookup so missing category ids produce the existing 404 response mapping.
+
+## Changes
+
+| File | Change | Notes |
+|------|--------|-------|
+| `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/category/CategoryServiceImpl.java` | modified | Removed product deletion; replace category memberships with a filtered set before category subtree deletion. |
+| `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/category/CategoryFacadeImpl.java` | modified | Use store-aware `getById` for deletion and 404 handling. |
+| `sm-core/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/catalog/CategoryTest.java` | added test | Verifies product preservation, mixed-category retention, and subtree category removal. |
+
+## Tests Added or Updated
+
+- `CategoryTest.deleteCategoryKeepsProductsAndDetachesSubtree` — products remain after category deletion, deleted memberships are removed, retained memberships remain, and root/child categories are gone.
+
+## Local Verification
+
+- Commands run: `mvn -q -pl sm-core -am -Dtest=CategoryTest -Dsurefire.failIfNoSpecifiedTests=false test` → passed.
+- Commands run: `mvn -q -pl sm-shop -am -DskipTests package` → passed.
+
+## Deviations from Assessment
+
+The integration fixture uses a persisted root category for the product association; no source scope was expanded.
+
+## Follow-ups
+
+- Add full HTTP/cart/order integration coverage when a reusable authenticated shop fixture is available.
